    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "Russia’s financial crisis unsettled investors. Apple had a new computer, Amazon was adding music, and Microsoft faced a disputed antitrust case.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The size of gains and losses along the path mattered as well as the endpoint. Owning one fast-changing business could create much sharper swings than holding cash.",
    "what_faded_away": "A product’s early sales and a legal headline did not give a complete five-year answer. No single story captured everything affecting a company.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "Nobody knew Amazon’s eventual result or the depth of the falls along the way. Its later fame can make a risky starting decision seem obvious in hindsight.",
